{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: model forecasts are systematically below realized prices, especially from ~day 10 onward. Apply an upward level shift that increases with horizon (small in days 1–5, larger in days 10–30).",
    "Trend/acceleration underreaction: when the market transitions from a dip to a rally, the model lags and fails to capture the upswing magnitude. Add a momentum term based on the last 5–10 days’ slope/return to steepen the forecast path.",
    "Horizon-dependent error growth: forecast errors widen with time; treat long-horizon outputs as too mean-reverting. Reduce mean-reversion strength and allow a higher terminal level when recent trend is positive.",
    "Upside tail miss: the model underestimates peak/rally days (late-horizon highs). Introduce an asymmetric correction: larger upward adjustment when recent volatility is rising and recent returns are positive.",
    "Post-dip rebound mispricing: after a sharp drawdown in the history window, the model expects only a mild recovery; realized outcomes show stronger rebound. If last-30d includes a notable trough and subsequent bounce, boost days 5–20 forecasts."
  ]
}
